        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Midway</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">4–7 June 1942; the Japanese Aleutian operation began a day earlier, on 3 June</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">The sea near Midway Atoll, about 1,300 miles (2,100 km) north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oahu">Oahu</a> in the Hawaiian chain, in the North Pacific</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Pacific Fleet under Admiral Chester Nimitz, with carrier groups under Frank Jack Fletcher and Raymond Spruance and 122 aircraft on Midway; the Japanese Combined Fleet under Admiral Isoroku Yamamoto, with the carrier strike force (Kidō Butai) under Chūichi Nagumo, which sailed with 248 aircraft on four carriers</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Japanese lost the carriers Akagi, Kaga, Sōryū and Hiryū and the heavy cruiser Mikuma, and 3,057 men; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> lost the carrier Yorktown, the destroyer Hammann and 307 men. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> did not take Midway.</span></div>
